web-build/
# Unanchored on purpose: any directory called android/ or ios/ is generated
# output. The consequence is that hand-written native sources must NOT live
# under a path segment with those names, or they are silently untracked —
# `git status` never lists them, so the omission is invisible. Keep Kotlin
# under a native/kotlin/ directory instead; see
# src/connections/google/native/kotlin/.
# Ignore only the root Expo generated projects. Local Expo modules keep their
# native sources under modules/*/android and modules/*/ios and MUST stay
# tracked, so these rules are anchored to the repository root.
/android/
/ios/
# Generated duplicate of the tracked src/connections/google/native/kotlin
# sources (the config plugin copies from native/kotlin into the build).
/src/connections/google/native/android/
*.log
.env
.DS_Store

# wrangler files
.wrangler
.dev.vars*
!.dev.vars.example
!.env.example
desktop.ini
bundletool-all.jar
kotleta552-release.jks
app.apks
application.aab